| Training Materials | User guides, video tutorials, example scripts | End of Week 11 |
| Knowledge Transfer Sessions | 3 interactive training sessions (2 hours each) | Week 12 |
| Final Project Report | Summary, metrics, recommendations | End of Week 12 |
## Page 4
4. ASSUMPTIONS & DEPENDENCIES
### 4.1 Assumptions
- Client will provide access to all existing TestStack.White codebases
- Test environments and applications under test will be available throughout the project
- Client team will be available for clarifications and validation
- All necessary licenses and tools will be provided by the client
- Current test data and test environments are stable and accessible
### 4.2 Dependencies
- Timely access to source code repositories
- Availability of subject matter experts from the client side
- Test environment availability during migration and testing phases
- Approval cycles will not exceed 3 business days
- No major application updates during the migration period
5. PROJECT TIMELINE
**Total Duration: 12 Weeks**
- **Weeks 1-2:** Assessment & Planning
- **Weeks 3-4:** Framework Development
- **Weeks 5-8:** Test Case Migration
- **Weeks 9-10:** Testing & Validation
- **Weeks 11-12:** Documentation & Knowledge Transfer
**Key Milestones:**
- Week 2: Migration strategy approved
- Week 4: Framework ready for migration
- Week 8: All scripts migrated
- Week 10: Validation complete
- Week 12: Project closure
## Page 5
6. ROLES & RESPONSIBILITIES
### 6.1 Vendor/Service Provider Responsibilities
- Provide experienced automation engineers for migration work
- Develop and deliver all project deliverables
- Conduct regular status meetings and progress updates
- Provide technical support during knowledge transfer period
- Deliver quality assurance for all migrated scripts
### 6.2 Client Responsibilities
- Provide access to existing codebase and documentation
- Make test environments and applications available
- Assign SMEs for knowledge sharing and validation
- Review and approve deliverables within agreed timelines
- Participate in training and knowledge transfer sessions
- Provide feedback and clarifications as needed
7. ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA
Each deliverable will be accepted based on the following criteria:
1. **Migrated Test Scripts:**
 - All existing test cases successfully converted to FlaUI
 - Test execution success rate ≥ 95%
 - No degradation in test coverage
 - Code follows agreed-upon standards
2. **Framework Architecture:**
 - Modular and maintainable code structure
 - Proper error handling and logging implemented
 - CI/CD integration functional
 - Performance meets or exceeds current framework
3. **Documentation:**
## Page 6
- Comprehensive and easy to understand
- Includes code examples and use cases
- Covers troubleshooting and FAQs
- Approved by client technical leads
4. Knowledge Transfer:
 - Team members can independently maintain scripts
 - Training session feedback scores ≥ 4/5
 - Q&A sessions completed
### 8. PAYMENT TERMS
**Total Project Cost:** [Insert Amount]
**Payment Schedule:**
- 20% upon SOW signing and project kickoff
- 30% upon completion of Phase 2 (Framework Development)
- 30% upon completion of Phase 3 (Test Case Migration)
- 20% upon final acceptance and project closure
**Payment Method:** [Specify method]
**Invoice Terms:** Net 30 days
### 9. CHANGE MANAGEMENT
Any changes to the scope, timeline, or deliverables must be documented through a formal Change Request process:
1. Change request submitted in writing
2. Impact analysis conducted (time, cost, resources)
3. Approval from both parties required
4. SOW amended with updated details
5. Work proceeds only after approval
## Page 7
10. RISK MANAGEMENT
| Risk | Impact | Mitigation Strategy |
|-------------------------------------------|--------|----------------------------------------------------------|
| Complex legacy code difficult to migrate | High | Early assessment, allocate buffer time |
| Test environment instability | Medium | Request stable environments, use test data snapshots |
| Key personnel unavailability | Medium | Cross-train team members, maintain documentation |
| Undocumented TestStack.White customizations | High | Conduct thorough code review, engage original developers |
| Application changes during migration | High | Freeze application updates during migration period |
11. TERMS & CONDITIONS
- All intellectual property created during this project belongs to the Client
- Both parties agree to maintain confidentiality of proprietary information
- This SOW is valid for 90 days from the date of issue
- Project governed by the Master Services Agreement between parties
- Either party may terminate with 30 days written notice with appropriate compensation
