## Page 1
STATEMENT OF WORK (SOW)
**UI Automation Framework Migration: TestStack.White to FlaUI**
**Document Version:** 1.0 
**Date:** December 5, 2025 
**Project Duration:** [Insert Duration] 
**Prepared For:** [Client Name] 
**Prepared By:** [Vendor/Team Name] 
----
### 1. PROJECT OVERVIEW
#### 1.1 Background
The current UI automation framework uses TestStack.White, which is no longer actively maintained and lacks support for modern Windows applications. This project will migrate the existing automation scripts and test cases to FlaUI, a modern and actively maintained UI automation library that provides better support for WPF, WinForms, Win32, and UWP applications.
#### 1.2 Objectives
- Migrate all existing TestStack.White automation scripts to FlaUI
- Modernize the test automation framework architecture
- Ensure all migrated test cases maintain or improve their reliability
- Provide comprehensive documentation for the new framework
- Train the team on FlaUI best practices
## Page 2
## 2. Scope of Work
### 2.1 In-Scope Activities
**Phase 1: Assessment & Planning (Week 1-2)**
- Conduct inventory of existing TestStack.White scripts and test cases
- Analyze dependencies and identify potential migration challenges
- Create detailed migration strategy and approach document
- Set up FlaUI development and test environments
- Define coding standards and framework architecture for FlaUI
**Phase 2: Framework Development (Week 3-4)**
- Design and implement base framework structure using FlaUI
- Create reusable component libraries and helper methods
- Implement logging, reporting, and error handling mechanisms
- Set up CI/CD pipeline integration for automated test execution
- Develop sample test scripts to validate framework functionality
**Phase 3: Test Case Migration (Week 5-8)**
- Migrate test scripts from TestStack.White to FlaUI
- Update element locators and interaction methods
- Refactor code to align with FlaUI best practices
- Implement parallel execution capabilities where applicable
- Create mapping document showing old vs. new implementations
**Phase 4: Testing & Validation (Week 9-10)**
- Execute all migrated test cases to verify functionality
- Perform comparative analysis of test execution times
- Identify and fix defects in migrated scripts
- Conduct regression testing across all application modules
- Performance benchmarking and optimization
## Page 3
Phase 5: Documentation & Knowledge Transfer (Week 11-12)
- Create comprehensive technical documentation
- Develop user guides and quick reference materials
- Conduct training sessions for QA team members
- Provide hands-on workshops for script maintenance
- Deliver final project report with lessons learned
2.2 Out-of-Scope
- Development of new test cases beyond existing coverage
- Application defect fixing (only test script issues will be addressed)
- Infrastructure upgrades beyond what's needed for FlaUI
- Migration of non-UI automation tests
- Performance testing or load testing activities
3. DELIVERABLES
| Deliverable | Description | Due Date |
|-------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------|----------------|
| Migration Strategy Document | Detailed approach, timeline, and risk assessment | End of Week 2 |
| FlaUI Framework Architecture | Base framework with core utilities and libraries | End of Week 4 |
| Migrated Test Scripts | All test cases converted to FlaUI | End of Week 8 |
| Test Execution Reports | Results from validation testing phase | End of Week 10 |
| Technical Documentation | Architecture, coding standards, troubleshooting guide | End of Week 11 |
| Training Materials | User guides, video tutorials, example scripts | End of Week 11 |
| Knowledge Transfer Sessions | 3 interactive training sessions (2 hours each) | Week 12 |
| Final Project Report | Summary, metrics, recommendations | End of Week 12 |
